  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Stamp of Origin",
    "overview": "The north star is the owner's chosen direction recorded in ADR-0006: stencilled produce crates and the rubber stamps of origin and grade on them, translated into a working interface for a shopper at the stall, on a phone. The world is ultramarine stamp ink on near-white label paper, stencil-black text, condensed heavy capitals for names and headings, and a plain humanist sans for everything that is read or operated. Stamp red is spent on one thing, the „Разгар“ (peak) level, and one marker yellow is reserved for the current month. Dark mode is its own scale, a deep ink-blue ground with lighter stamp inks, not an inversion.\n\nThe world is calm by decision. Capitals appear only in headings and (once built) stamps, the surfaces are flat, separation comes from hairline rules, and there is no motion beyond the global reduced-motion guard. Density is moderate: the content column is capped at 72rem, prose at 42rem, and sections are separated by 2–4rem.\n\nThis file describes the system as built after slice 1 (spec 022, tokens and typography). The palette, the faces and the global heading styles are shipped. The components below still carry their pre-redesign layouts, now rendered in the new tokens; the shell (#92), the season stamp and year strip (#93), the produce page (#94) and the data visuals (#95) are later slices. Anything marked **planned** is decided in ADR-0006 but not yet in the code. Tokens are generated from `src/design/tokens.ts` and inlined as CSS custom properties (`--color-*`, `--space-*`, `--font-size-*`, `--radius-*`, and others); light values sit on `:root` and dark values override them under `prefers-color-scheme: dark`.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Sofia Sans Extra Condensed 800 in capitals for headings; Sofia Sans for body, navigation, lists and tables.",
      "Latin names in Sofia Sans italic 400, through the global `[lang='la']` rule.",
      "Ultramarine ink on label paper; stamp red only for „Разгар“; marker yellow only for the current month.",
      "Season level = fill + SVG mark + Bulgarian text label, never colour alone.",
      "Flat surfaces and hairline rules, no shadows, no motion.",
      "One small corner radius (0.375rem) on every rounded element.",
      "Touch targets of at least 2.75rem on primary links and controls."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Red Means Разгар Rule",
        "body": "Stamp red is the „Разгар“ level and nothing else: not errors, not links, not emphasis. Text on it is always `on-peak`.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Marker Rule",
        "body": "Marker yellow marks the current month and nothing else. It is a fill with `on-marker` text, never a line or a text colour on the light page.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tested Pair Rule",
        "body": "A colour is used on a background only when that pair is in the tested contrast set. Components take colours from tokens only and contain no literal colours.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Capitals Are Headings Rule",
        "body": "Sofia Sans Extra Condensed in capitals is for the logo, `h1`–`h3` and (planned, #93) stamps. Capitals come from `text-transform`, so the source text and reading order are unchanged without CSS. Body, navigation, lists and tables stay in Sofia Sans, in sentence case.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Weight Rule",
        "body": "The condensed face exists at 800 only. Never set it at another weight or in italic; the browser would synthesise it.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every table uses `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink On Paper Rule",
        "body": "Surfaces never lift. A panel is set apart by its tone or a hairline, never by a shadow or gradient.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do take every colour, space step, font size and radius from the custom properties generated by `src/design/tokens.ts`, and add every new colour pair to `tests/fixtures/contrastPairs.ts`.",
      "Do show the season level as fill (or, from #93, stamp form) + `LevelMark` + text label; use `on-peak` on stamp red and `on-badge` on the washes.",
      "Do set headings in Sofia Sans Extra Condensed 800 through the global `h1`–`h3` rule, and mark Latin names with `lang=\"la\"` so they render in Sofia Sans italic.",
      "Do keep links and controls at least 2.75rem tall (`--target-min`), with the 3px `focus` outline (`focus-on-shell` inside the shell).",
      "Do cap prose at `--reading-width` (42rem) and the page at `--content-width` (72rem).",
      "Do use `rule` for decorative hairlines and `border` for control and data boundaries."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use stamp red for anything but „Разгар“, or marker yellow for anything but the current month.",
      "Don't set body text, navigation, lists or tables in the condensed face or in capitals.",
      "Don't add shadows, gradients or elevated surfaces, and don't add motion beyond the reduced-motion guard.",
      "Don't tilt stamps in lists; only the large stamp at the top of the produce page is tilted.",
      "Don't convey the season level by colour alone.",
      "Don't add prices, calls to buy or shop styling to produce; the stamps mark origin and season, not a sale.",
      "Don't use `rule` for text or control boundaries; it is below 3:1 by design.",
      "Don't reorder content with CSS. Pages must read in source order without styles."
    ]
  }
}
